  "id": "bird-dog",
  "name": "Bird Dog",
  "definition": "A quadruped alternating contralateral arm-and-leg extension drill. Shoulder flexion, scapular upward rotation, hip extension and knee extension lift the free limbs while the contacted hand and opposite knee support the body. The trunk resists extension and rotation rather than performing a crunch or twist. Abs and obliques are primary for that core-control intent; deltoid, serratus, gluteal and knee-extensor roles are bounded anatomy-and-mechanics inferences, not measured recruitment rankings. Lumbar extensors control spinal posture but do not create deliberate spinal extension. The app credits this extensor system without painting unrelated back meshes. Standing, weighted, same-side, elbow-to-knee crunch and timed-only variants remain excluded.",
